  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Iron Bow Technologies obligated $297M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Iron Bow Technologies won 397 awards so far this fiscal year, and the average award size is $749K. Iron Bow Technologies obligations are down 37.1% year over year. Yearly obligations climbed from $513M in FY21 to $706M in FY24, then fell to $472M in FY25 before reaching $297M in FY26 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $238M to Iron Bow Technologies in FY2026 to date. The Department of Transportation obligated $58.5M, and the Smithsonian Institution obligated $601K. Iron Bow Technologies largest markets in FY2026 to date are Other Computer Related Services at $120M, Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing at $101M, and Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $72.2M. The current-year totals are partial because FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers of Iron Bow Technologies?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $238M to Iron Bow Technologies in FY2026 to date. The Department of Transportation obligated $58.5M, and the Smithsonian Institution obligated $601K. Other buyers in the top ten include the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission at $436K, the Department of Veterans Affairs at $426K, and the U.S. Agency for Global Media at $197K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What principal markets does Iron Bow Technologies serve?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest market for Iron Bow Technologies at $120M in FY2026 to date. Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing follows at $101M, and Electronic Computer Manufacturing is $72.2M. Additional market lines include Software Publishers at $2.6M and Computer and Computer Peripheral Equipment and Software Merchant Wholesalers at $601K."
      }
    ]
  },
